<DocsLayout title="Docker">
  <h1>Run with Docker</h1>
  <p>Identity ships as a multi-arch image (linux/amd64, linux/arm64) at <code>ghcr.io/elloloop/identity</code>.</p>

  <h2>Pull a release</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">docker pull ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:latest
# Or pin a version
docker pull ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0</code></pre>
  <p>Tags are produced from semver git tags (<code>v0.1.0</code>) by <code>.github/workflows/release.yml</code>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>0.1.0</code> &mdash; full version</li>
    <li><code>0.1</code> &mdash; major.minor</li>
    <li><code>0</code> &mdash; major</li>
    <li><code>latest</code> &mdash; only set for non-prerelease tags</li>
    <li><code>sha-&lt;commit&gt;</code> &mdash; per-commit pin</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Minimal run</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">docker run -d --name identity \
  -p 80:80 -p 9090:9090 \
  -e GATEWAY_ENTDB_ADDRESS=entdb:50051 \
  -e GATEWAY_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID=my-product \
  ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:latest</code></pre>
  <p>Identity will boot with an auto-generated dev RSA key and log a warning. That works for kicking the tires; for anything real, supply <code>GATEWAY_JWT_KEYS</code>.</p>

  <h2>Production run</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">docker run -d --name identity \
  -p 80:80 -p 9090:9090 \
  -e GATEWAY_ENTDB_ADDRESS=entdb.internal:50051 \
  -e GATEWAY_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID=my-product \
  -e GATEWAY_JWT_KEYS="$(cat keyring.json)" \
  -e GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_ID=app.my-product.com \
  -e GATEWAY_PASSKEY_ORIGIN=https://app.my-product.com \
  -e GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_NAME="My Product" \
  -e GATEWAY_TOTP_ISSUER="My Product" \
  -e GATEWAY_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY="$(openssl rand -base64 32)" \
  -e GATEWAY_DEFAULT_EMAIL_DOMAIN=my-product.com \
  -e GATEWAY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS="https://app.my-product.com,https://admin.my-product.com" \
  -e GATEWAY_COOKIE_SECURE=true \
  -e GATEWAY_AUTH_ALLOW_LOCAL=true \
  ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0</code></pre>

  <Callout type="warning" title="TOTP encryption key must be 32 bytes base64">
    On startup Identity decodes <code>GATEWAY_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> with base64 and expects exactly 32 bytes; anything else is a fatal error. <code>openssl rand -base64 32</code> produces a 32-byte key.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Ports</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Port</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Env var</th></tr>
    <tr><td>80</td><td>Connect-RPC + JWKS + health</td><td><code>GATEWAY_CONNECT_PORT</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>9090</td><td>Prometheus <code>/metrics</code></td><td><code>GATEWAY_METRICS_PORT</code></td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>The <code>EXPOSE</code> directive in the image declares both. The container runs as a non-root user (distroless <code>nonroot</code>).</p>

  <h2>Image internals</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Base: <code>gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot</code> (pinned by digest)</li>
    <li>Binary: <code>/bin/identity</code></li>
    <li>Build flags: <code>CGO_ENABLED=0</code>, <code>-ldflags "-s -w"</code></li>
    <li>Entrypoint: <code>/bin/identity</code> (no shell)</li>
    <li>Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64</li>
    <li>SBOM and provenance attestations attached at release time</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Health probes</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash"># Liveness / readiness — same endpoint
curl -fsS http://localhost/health
# {"status":"ok"}</code></pre>

  <h2>Verifying the image</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">docker pull ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0
docker image inspect ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0 \
  --format '{{.Os}}/{{.Architecture}} {{.Config.Entrypoint}}'</code></pre>

